1 OCCU Kungamakaren Carl Otto Mörner, Överste, 1829-41 tullinspektor vid Blockhusudden, Öfverste
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Carl Otto Mörner af Mörlanda=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baron''' [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Otto_M%C3%B6rnerr '''''Carl'' Otto Mörner'''] was a Swedish courtier, and member of the Diet. He is chiefly remembered for his role in advocating for Frenchman [https://en.wikipedi
2 CONC a.org/wiki/Charles_XIV_John '''Jean Baptiste Bernadotte''']'s succession to the Swedish crown in 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Role in the succession to Charles XIII of Sweden===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1810 King''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIII '''Charles XIII'''] of Sweden was childless and the crown prince [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_August,_Crown_Prince_of_Sweden '''Charles August'''] had died o
2 CONC f a stroke. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baron Mörner, entirely''' on his own initiative, offered the succession to the Swedish crown to Bernadotte. Although the Swedish government, amazed at Mörner's effrontery, placed him under arrest, the candidature of Bernadotte 
2 CONC gradually gained favor and on 21 August 1810 in Örebro Bernadotte was elected by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riksdag_of_the_Estates Riksdag of the Estates] to be the new Crown Prince, and was subsequently made Generalissimu
2 CONC s of the Swedish Armed Forces by the King. He was crowned [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIV_John '''Charles XIV of Sweden'''] on 5 February 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===In film===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baron Mörner is a''' character in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%A9sir%C3%A9e_(film%29 Désirée], a 1954 historical film biography. The film tells a fictionalized story of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%A9sir%C3%A9e_Cl
2 CONC ary '''Désirée Clary'''], spouse of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIV_John '''Charles XIV of Sweden'''], and her relationship with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon '''Napoleon'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
