1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://dokumente.ios-regensburg.de/amburger/index.php?id=79229
2 CONT
2 CONT "Baron Anton von Taube from the House of Poidifer in Estonia. Born in 1787, died in 1848 as a retired Colonel as Junker on the Chevalier Garde Regiment, he took part in the Battle of Austerlitz in 1805, 1807 as Cornet in the Sumy 
2 CONC Regiment the Battle of Preussisch-Eylau. He also served with distinction in the wars of liberation as a Sumy Hussar. He is the father of the earlier Governor-General of Omsk, at present, a member of the Imperial Council Baron Maxi
2 CONC m Taube. Anton von Taube is often mentioned in these memoirs." /"With Count Pahlen´s Cavalry against Napoleon: Memoirs of the Russian General Eduard von Löwenstern (1790-1837)"
