1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "'''Reinhold Adolphe Louis Stackelberg''', born 1822, died 1871 was a Swedish Count , landowner and industrialist and one of the Småland revival movement enthusiasts.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Adolphe Stackelberg was born in a grevligt home, however, lacked consider more wealth. Despite this, Adolphe Stackelberg get permission to marry the very wealthy baron JK Adelswärd's daughter Honorine. This was August 30, 1847. B
2 CONC aron Adelswärd gave the couple Stensnäs mansion with associated farms. Adolphe Stackelberg was a very religious man, and began early to think about how he could ensure their workers soul merchandise in the best way. He began to ho
2 CONC ld prayer times increasingly circuits and invited home spiritual speakers of different kinds. This gave Stackelberg nicknamed "reader Count".
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1852, Count Stackelberg met for the first time revivalist preacher Carl Olof Rosenius which marked the start of a lifelong friendship. In 1854 they established a joint Assembly in Vastervik . In the autumn of 1855 also began t
2 CONC he evangelical revival in Kalmar to organize themselves in mission compounds. This was the beginning of Östra Småland missionary association .
2 CONT
2 CONT "1860 inherited Stackelberg also Överums bruk of their in-laws. There, he had to start with building a "mobile church" that could be moved around on the gratings. In the years 1865-1867 preached a certain Nicolaus Bergensköld whic
2 CONC h would later emigrate to the United States and which became a leading figure in the Swedish countryside missionary movement . Later Stackelberg also built a permanent church to use the square. This, however, was not completed unt
2 CONC il after his death and was consecrated August 18, 1872."
2 CONT
